1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,069
Naruto Uzumaki learned a forbidden jutsu in one night, and read one line too many.

2
00:00:06,069 --> 00:00:08,789
Everything his clones learn, he keeps.

3
00:00:09,007 --> 00:00:14,237
Then he read the Hokage's whole archive and found a roster with one name inked out.

4
00:00:14,237 --> 00:00:16,316
He already knows which name fits.

5
00:00:16,558 --> 00:00:20,624
The next morning, every chair in the Hokage's office is taken.

6
00:00:20,624 --> 00:00:23,247
So is the windowsill. So is the ceiling.

7
00:00:23,485 --> 00:00:26,174
[NARUTO] Old man. Who was Kushina Uzumaki?

8
00:00:29,122 --> 00:00:31,732
The old man doesn't answer for a long time.

9
00:00:31,732 --> 00:00:35,191
The pipe in his hand has gone out, and he hasn't noticed.

10
00:00:35,442 --> 00:00:37,871
[HIRUZEN] Which one of you is the real one?

11
00:00:37,989 --> 00:00:39,683
[NARUTO] The one who's not sitting in your hat.

12
00:00:39,829 --> 00:00:41,328
[CLONE] I'm in the hat, if that helps.

13
00:00:41,471 --> 00:00:43,320
[HIRUZEN] Who told you that name?

14
00:00:43,462 --> 00:00:47,765
[NARUTO] Nobody. That's the problem. Everybody I asked changed the subject.

15
00:00:47,765 --> 00:00:51,611
[NARUTO] The shelf, the roster, my birthday. Even the dust is lying.

16
00:00:51,764 --> 00:00:55,421
Twelve years ago, the Third Hokage made a law.

17
00:00:55,421 --> 00:01:02,893
Nobody in Konoha may speak of the Nine-Tails inside Naruto. Not to him, and not to their kids.

18
00:01:03,122 --> 00:01:04,231
Everybody obeyed.

19
00:01:04,231 --> 00:01:10,361
It's the loneliest law the village ever wrote, and the man who wrote it is sitting very still.

20
00:01:10,597 --> 00:01:17,206
[HIRUZEN] I made that law. I can break it. I'm only asking myself whether I should.

21
00:01:17,322 --> 00:01:19,851
[CLONE] There's a thousand of us, old man. Sixty in here.

22
00:01:19,851 --> 00:01:24,341
[CLONE] The rest are in the corridor, the garden and on the roof. Every one of us is listening.

23
00:01:24,492 --> 00:01:27,915
Ears are pressed to every window of the Hokage Tower.

24
00:01:27,915 --> 00:01:31,661
A thousand Narutos, holding their breath at the same time.

25
00:01:31,907 --> 00:01:36,813
The old man has been lying for twelve years, for reasons he thought were good.

26
00:01:36,813 --> 00:01:41,531
Now he's counting his audience. A lie only works on one listener at a time.

27
00:01:41,769 --> 00:01:47,110
[HIRUZEN] Your mother was Kushina Uzumaki. Red hair, down to her waist.

28
00:01:47,110 --> 00:01:51,488
[HIRUZEN] And a temper the whole village learned to respect.

29
00:01:51,630 --> 00:01:52,614
[NARUTO] She had red hair?

30
00:01:52,759 --> 00:01:57,268
[HIRUZEN] Very red. You got her stubbornness. Not her hair.

31
00:01:57,396 --> 00:02:01,799
Before Naruto, the Nine-Tails lived inside Kushina Uzumaki.

32
00:02:01,799 --> 00:02:06,800
That part isn't a what-if. It's the first thing the old man admits.

33
00:02:07,059 --> 00:02:12,903
[HIRUZEN] And your father was Minato Namikaze. The Fourth Hokage.

34
00:02:13,018 --> 00:02:17,467
The Fourth Hokage. The face on the mountain, right outside the window.

35
00:02:17,467 --> 00:02:22,932
Naruto once painted that face orange. He did it with a bucket and a lot of confidence.

36
00:02:23,135 --> 00:02:24,134
[NARUTO] I painted my dad.

37
00:02:24,244 --> 00:02:28,823
[HIRUZEN] You painted him with great enthusiasm. He would have laughed.

38
00:02:28,964 --> 00:02:37,201
Then the old man tells the rest. October tenth. The seal weakened as Naruto was born, and the fox got loose over the village.

39
00:02:37,201 --> 00:02:41,353
The Fourth fought it, and sealed it inside his own newborn son.

40
00:02:41,563 --> 00:02:45,646
Neither parent lived to see morning. The old man says it plainly.

41
00:02:45,646 --> 00:02:48,662
If he's telling the truth, he'll tell all of it.

42
00:02:48,878 --> 00:02:49,802
[NARUTO] How did it get out?

43
00:02:49,931 --> 00:02:55,195
[HIRUZEN] The seal weakens in childbirth. That's all anyone knows.

44
00:02:55,339 --> 00:02:58,545
The old man braces for shouting. It doesn't come.

45
00:02:58,545 --> 00:03:03,648
Naruto has spent a month reading what happens to people who panic. He doesn't.

46
00:03:03,868 --> 00:03:05,057
[NARUTO] Why didn't you tell me?

47
00:03:05,178 --> 00:03:11,141
[HIRUZEN] Because the village feared the fox, and children repeat what their parents say.

48
00:03:11,141 --> 00:03:16,122
[HIRUZEN] I thought silence would keep you safe. I was wrong about the cost.

49
00:03:16,275 --> 00:03:21,533
Nobody moves. Sixty Narutos have stopped fidgeting for the first time in their lives.

50
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:25,059
One of them is holding the old man's hat, very carefully.

51
00:03:25,259 --> 00:03:26,143
[CLONE] We're here, Boss.

52
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:30,804
[NARUTO] I'm not gonna yell, old man. I want two things. First, don't lie to me again.

53
00:03:30,948 --> 00:03:33,797
[HIRUZEN] Never again. And the second?

54
00:03:33,936 --> 00:03:37,175
[NARUTO] Mom and Dad's mission reports. Everything they ever filed.

55
00:03:37,308 --> 00:03:39,477
[HIRUZEN] Those are classified.

56
00:03:39,632 --> 00:03:41,671
[NARUTO] I'm on staff. There's a form.

57
00:03:41,801 --> 00:03:43,705
[CLONE] Section whatever! He signed it twice!

58
00:03:43,861 --> 00:03:47,515
[HIRUZEN] I did write that form myself, didn't I.

59
00:03:47,662 --> 00:03:50,195
No shouting. No revenge. No apology.

60
00:03:50,195 --> 00:03:57,021
Naruto has just learned who his parents were, and the first thing he asks for is their paperwork.

61
00:03:59,959 --> 00:04:06,396
Midnight, in the archive. A thousand clones would be too loud, so it's twenty.

62
00:04:06,396 --> 00:04:10,523
Two boxes on the back table. Namikaze. Uzumaki, K.

63
00:04:10,771 --> 00:04:11,440
[NARUTO] You open it.

64
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:13,454
[CLONE] I'm you. I'm also not ready.

65
00:04:13,599 --> 00:04:14,803
[NARUTO] Then we'll open it together.

66
00:04:14,936 --> 00:04:16,490
[CLONE] Okay. On three.

67
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,584
[NARUTO] On three, or after three?

68
00:04:18,726 --> 00:04:20,780
[CLONE] Why is that hard?! Just open it!

69
00:04:20,917 --> 00:04:26,545
The Fourth Hokage's reports are dry, exact and short. Departure time. Route.

70
00:04:26,545 --> 00:04:31,951
Enemy strength. Result. He never uses an adjective when a number will do.

71
00:04:32,182 --> 00:04:35,231
[CLONE] Listen to this one. Mission complete. Zero casualties.

72
00:04:35,231 --> 00:04:38,901
[CLONE] Zero damage to client property. Client unhappy about the weather.

73
00:04:38,831 --> 00:04:40,705
[CLONE] Here's another. Mission complete.

74
00:04:40,705 --> 00:04:44,510
[CLONE] Cause of delay, council meeting. Cause of council meeting, unknown.

75
00:04:44,653 --> 00:04:46,732
[NARUTO] He's so boring. I love him already.

76
00:04:46,874 --> 00:04:51,503
[CLONE] Boss. Border patrol report. It says, nothing happened. Underlined.

77
00:04:51,614 --> 00:04:54,423
[NARUTO] He was proud of nothing. Best sentence ever.

78
00:04:54,583 --> 00:05:00,584
Then, in the margin of a patrol report, the only thing in the box that isn't a number.

79
00:05:00,584 --> 00:05:04,492
A doodle. A small steaming bowl, with chopsticks. Ramen.

80
00:05:04,750 --> 00:05:07,949
[CLONE] Boss. He drew ramen. On a patrol report.

81
00:05:08,084 --> 00:05:09,033
[NARUTO] Of course he did.

82
00:05:09,156 --> 00:05:10,730
[CLONE] Boss, are you crying?

83
00:05:10,848 --> 00:05:13,382
[NARUTO] It's dust. This whole archive is dust.

84
00:05:13,517 --> 00:05:18,237
His father's capital letters lean forward, like he's late for something.

85
00:05:18,237 --> 00:05:23,481
Naruto's do too. He's never noticed. He's never had anything to compare them to.

86
00:05:23,731 --> 00:05:27,316
Kushina's box is thicker. It's an incident file.

87
00:05:27,316 --> 00:05:32,470
Every wall, fence and window she ever broke, in order, with invoices.

88
00:05:32,689 --> 00:05:36,779
[CLONE] Broken fence, market district. Broken door, Academy.

89
00:05:36,779 --> 00:05:39,453
[CLONE] Broken wall, the same wall, twice.

90
00:05:39,383 --> 00:05:42,206
[CLONE] Cause of damage, temper. Cause of damage, temper.

91
00:05:42,206 --> 00:05:45,317
[CLONE] Cause of damage, temper, but the other man started it.

92
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:48,414
[NARUTO] Cause of damage, temper. That's my mom.

93
00:05:48,653 --> 00:05:51,191
It's the first time he's ever spoken the word.

94
00:05:51,191 --> 00:05:54,557
It comes out as a joke, so it won't have to be anything else.

95
00:05:54,794 --> 00:05:57,623
[CLONE] Boss, there's a fountain. She broke a fountain.

96
00:05:57,742 --> 00:05:58,716
[NARUTO] How did she do that?

97
00:05:58,834 --> 00:06:01,603
[CLONE] It says she was practising something. The fountain was in the way.

98
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:04,050
[NARUTO] The fountain was in the way. That's so true.

99
00:06:04,185 --> 00:06:07,508
[CLONE] Last page. A man said something rude about her friend.

100
00:06:07,508 --> 00:06:09,724
[CLONE] Damages paid in full. Apology, none.

101
00:06:09,842 --> 00:06:11,856
[NARUTO] Good. Nobody should apologise for that.

102
00:06:12,004 --> 00:06:13,153
[CLONE] Can we frame the invoices?

103
00:06:13,265 --> 00:06:15,269
[NARUTO] No. We're framing the invoices.

104
00:06:15,397 --> 00:06:19,715
Clerks say a person's file is who they were on their worst day.

105
00:06:19,715 --> 00:06:24,856
Kushina's worst days, Naruto notices, were nearly always for somebody else.

106
00:06:25,068 --> 00:06:27,706
By morning he has met both of his parents.

107
00:06:27,706 --> 00:06:35,242
One was careful, one was loud, and neither of them got to file a report about him. He'll have to write that one himself.

108
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:42,184
Deeper in the box there's another set of reports. About a team.

109
00:06:42,184 --> 00:06:46,944
Three genin and one jonin, written up every week in the same dry hand.

110
00:06:47,197 --> 00:06:50,961
[CLONE] Boss. His students. One of them is called Kakashi Hatake.

111
00:06:51,078 --> 00:06:52,002
[NARUTO] Our Kakashi?

112
00:06:52,146 --> 00:06:55,345
[CLONE] Skilled. Follows every rule. Will need to learn which ones matter.

113
00:06:55,480 --> 00:07:00,896
Team Minato. Kakashi, a boy named Obito Uchiha, and a girl named Rin Nohara.

114
00:07:00,896 --> 00:07:07,239
Their teacher writes about them like they're the most interesting things he's ever filed.

115
00:07:07,479 --> 00:07:09,705
[CLONE] Obito Uchiha. Late every single day.

116
00:07:09,705 --> 00:07:15,083
[CLONE] Reason given, helped an old woman across the road. Every report. A different old woman.

117
00:07:15,212 --> 00:07:16,976
[NARUTO] A different old woman. Huh.

118
00:07:17,094 --> 00:07:20,255
Naruto has heard excuses like that. This week.

119
00:07:20,255 --> 00:07:24,173
From a man with a book, who got lost on the road of life.

120
00:07:24,428 --> 00:07:25,582
[NARUTO] He learned it from Obito.

121
00:07:25,730 --> 00:07:32,348
He opens his notebook to the eleven dates. Then he finds the last pages of the team's file.

122
00:07:32,348 --> 00:07:37,439
Two names. Two dates. Two short reports, as dry and exact as the rest.

123
00:07:37,658 --> 00:07:39,397
[CLONE] Boss. The dates match.

124
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:41,309
[NARUTO] I know. I counted twice.

125
00:07:41,458 --> 00:07:43,047
[CLONE] Boss. Do we tell the others?

126
00:07:43,181 --> 00:07:45,415
[NARUTO] Tell them what? It's not our name to tell.

127
00:07:45,566 --> 00:07:48,672
Eleven clerks noted that Kakashi was late.

128
00:07:48,672 --> 00:07:52,295
Nobody wrote down why, because nobody ever asked.

129
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:59,108
The next dawn. Team Seven waits at the training ground. Sasuke glares at the trees.

130
00:07:59,108 --> 00:08:05,299
Sakura reads the clouds. Kakashi Hatake is late, as always. Every single time.

131
00:08:05,555 --> 00:08:07,414
[SAKURA] He said dawn. It's noon.

132
00:08:07,537 --> 00:08:11,736
[SASUKE] He's asleep in a tree somewhere. Ignore him and train.

133
00:08:11,873 --> 00:08:15,342
[NARUTO] Give me an hour. Do the wall drill. Don't touch my wires.

134
00:08:15,476 --> 00:08:16,325
[SAKURA] Where are you going?

135
00:08:16,457 --> 00:08:17,586
[NARUTO] To read something.

136
00:08:17,738 --> 00:08:24,410
Past the training grounds stands a black stone covered in names. Every ninja on it died for the village.

137
00:08:24,410 --> 00:08:29,607
One man stands before it, hands in his pockets, reading a name he knows by heart.

138
00:08:29,816 --> 00:08:33,890
In canon, this is why Kakashi is late. Not laziness. A name.

139
00:08:33,890 --> 00:08:38,915
It's the one place in Konoha where he can talk to someone who isn't there.

140
00:08:39,153 --> 00:08:42,162
[KAKASHI] Eleven reports. You counted, didn't you.

141
00:08:42,283 --> 00:08:45,896
Naruto doesn't answer. He walks up and stands next to him.

142
00:08:45,896 --> 00:08:50,382
He's read a lot of names this month. He's never stood this close to one.

143
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,829
[KAKASHI] Don't say anything. Please.

144
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:58,201
So Naruto says nothing. A month ago he'd have read the names out loud.

145
00:08:58,201 --> 00:09:02,403
Today he knows better. Some names you just stand beside.

146
00:09:02,609 --> 00:09:05,336
[KAKASHI] Thanks. Go on. I'll be right behind you.

147
00:09:05,491 --> 00:09:10,345
He is. It takes him an hour. Then he strolls in like nothing has happened.

148
00:09:10,586 --> 00:09:16,316
[KAKASHI] Sorry I'm late. A black cat crossed my path, so I took the long way.

149
00:09:16,476 --> 00:09:18,520
[SAKURA] Liar! There are no black cats!

150
00:09:18,673 --> 00:09:20,287
[SASUKE] Liar. Obviously.

151
00:09:20,410 --> 00:09:22,474
[NARUTO] Leave him alone. Go do the wall drill.

152
00:09:22,584 --> 00:09:26,911
Nobody on Team Seven asks why, and Naruto never tells them.

153
00:09:26,911 --> 00:09:32,118
Some things don't go in a file. He keeps this one next to Iruka's face.

154
00:09:35,011 --> 00:09:41,568
That night, Naruto goes looking for what has lived in him since birth. A flooded corridor.

155
00:09:41,568 --> 00:09:47,250
Dark water. A gate taller than a house, held shut by one small strip of paper.

156
00:09:47,454 --> 00:09:51,672
He brings one clone and one book. A beginner's chakra control primer.

157
00:09:51,672 --> 00:09:55,523
It's the only book he's never been thrown out of a library for.

158
00:09:55,753 --> 00:10:01,617
[KURAMA] Twelve years I listened to you snore. I never expected you to knock.

159
00:10:01,759 --> 00:10:05,293
[NARUTO] You said her name. Kushina. You lived in her.

160
00:10:05,425 --> 00:10:10,824
[KURAMA] It was cramped. She talked in her sleep. I wouldn't call it a friendship.

161
00:10:10,970 --> 00:10:15,393
Twelve years in the dark. Fed on nothing, spoken to by no one.

162
00:10:15,393 --> 00:10:20,029
And in all that time, nobody has ever asked if the fox was bored.

163
00:10:20,261 --> 00:10:26,930
[KURAMA] Say what you want, brat. Nobody comes down here unless they want something.

164
00:10:27,076 --> 00:10:30,545
[NARUTO] October tenth. You were there. I want what you remember.

165
00:10:30,689 --> 00:10:35,463
[KURAMA] A memory. And what do I get for it? Your face?

166
00:10:35,617 --> 00:10:37,166
[NARUTO] A book. Just a book.

167
00:10:37,278 --> 00:10:38,672
[KURAMA] I don't read.

168
00:10:38,828 --> 00:10:42,792
[NARUTO] You were reading the whole time. You said so. Did you think I wasn't reading too?

169
00:10:42,930 --> 00:10:44,276
The fox doesn't answer.

170
00:10:44,276 --> 00:10:51,709
For a creature who has spent centuries flattening mountains, he looks, for one moment, exactly like a customer caught browsing.

171
00:10:51,951 --> 00:10:55,765
[KURAMA] One chapter. If it's bad, you leave.

172
00:10:55,890 --> 00:11:00,621
A clone sits down in the dark water before the largest cage in the world.

173
00:11:00,621 --> 00:11:06,064
Nobody asks how a clone gets in here. It's his own head. Mostly he's stopped asking.

174
00:11:06,294 --> 00:11:11,363
[CLONE] Chapter one. Chakra is the union of physical energy and spiritual energy.

175
00:11:11,507 --> 00:11:14,206
[KURAMA] Wrong. Obviously wrong.

176
00:11:14,364 --> 00:11:15,403
[CLONE] It's the first sentence!

177
00:11:15,552 --> 00:11:19,761
[KURAMA] Then the author has never met any. Continue.

178
00:11:19,882 --> 00:11:23,645
He gets through three pages. The fox corrects four errors.

179
00:11:23,645 --> 00:11:28,186
Somewhere in the village, a tired boy is copying them into his margin.

180
00:11:28,402 --> 00:11:30,846
[CLONE] Page nine says a beginner should aim for balance.

181
00:11:31,003 --> 00:11:38,532
[KURAMA] Page nine was written by someone who has never held anything. Read it again. Slower.

182
00:11:38,643 --> 00:11:43,255
By the third night the fox has stopped saying wrong and started saying again.

183
00:11:43,255 --> 00:11:48,407
A creature of pure hatred, listening to a beginner's primer. He'd sooner eat the book.

184
00:11:48,662 --> 00:11:52,361
[CLONE] Chapter two. Chakra control is the foundation of all ninja arts.

185
00:11:52,481 --> 00:11:58,698
[KURAMA] Chakra control is the foundation of not dying. Write that down.

186
00:11:58,822 --> 00:12:00,911
[CLONE] Boss, he wants us to write that down.

187
00:12:01,041 --> 00:12:02,230
[NARUTO] Then write it down.

188
00:12:02,387 --> 00:12:05,036
[KURAMA] Is there a villain in this book?

189
00:12:05,184 --> 00:12:08,123
[CLONE] It's a chakra primer. The villain is poor posture.

190
00:12:08,242 --> 00:12:11,506
[KURAMA] Hm. Poor posture. Continue.

191
00:12:11,653 --> 00:12:15,842
[KURAMA] You still want it. The night of the red sky.

192
00:12:16,001 --> 00:12:17,385
[NARUTO] Yes. All of it.

193
00:12:17,519 --> 00:12:23,104
[KURAMA] I remember being angry. I've been angry for a very long time.

194
00:12:23,104 --> 00:12:26,583
[KURAMA] But that night, the anger wasn't mine.

195
00:12:26,710 --> 00:12:27,484
[NARUTO] What does that mean?

196
00:12:27,602 --> 00:12:32,633
[KURAMA] A man in a mask. One red eye in the hole of it.

197
00:12:32,633 --> 00:12:37,021
[KURAMA] And my own will, going out like a candle.

198
00:12:37,605 --> 00:12:38,149
[NARUTO] That's it?

199
00:12:38,301 --> 00:12:45,525
[KURAMA] That's all I'll give you. One true memory. You want another, bring a better book.

200
00:12:45,677 --> 00:12:47,491
[NARUTO] I'm not doing this because I like you.

201
00:12:47,650 --> 00:12:50,289
[KURAMA] Good. I'd be insulted.

202
00:12:50,414 --> 00:12:57,921
The clone pops. Across the village, Naruto sits up in the dark holding a memory that isn't his. A mask.

203
00:12:57,921 --> 00:13:06,083
A fox who didn't choose. The seal didn't just break. Somebody was there. And that isn't in any file in the Leaf.

204
00:13:06,308 --> 00:13:11,042
[KURAMA] Tomorrow, brat. And bring a book with a villain who wins.

205
00:13:13,592 --> 00:13:15,522
Somebody else has noticed.

206
00:13:15,522 --> 00:13:24,951
Danzo, the Third's oldest rival, hears of a boy with the Nine-Tails, a jutsu that copies his mind, and the keys to the archive.

207
00:13:25,154 --> 00:13:28,925
To the Third, it's a lonely child with a filing job.

208
00:13:28,925 --> 00:13:32,768
To Danzo, it's a weapon left unattended in a library.

209
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:38,081
Two in the morning. A man in a plain white mask walks into the archive.

210
00:13:38,081 --> 00:13:43,140
No village crest. No footsteps. He heads straight for the Namikaze box.

211
00:13:43,385 --> 00:13:47,465
By the shelf stands a filing box. It's been there since yesterday.

212
00:13:47,465 --> 00:13:52,164
Nobody asked why. It's a clone, and it's having the worst shift of its life.

213
00:13:52,398 --> 00:13:55,767
[CLONE] Do not move. You're a box. Boxes don't have opinions.

214
00:13:55,697 --> 00:13:59,681
[CLONE] He's reading the Uzumaki file. Why is he reading the Uzumaki file?

215
00:13:59,611 --> 00:14:02,300
[CLONE] He's writing in a little book. Boss is gonna want that little book.

216
00:14:02,230 --> 00:14:06,514
[CLONE] He's counting the boxes. There are forty. I'm number forty one. I don't match.

217
00:14:06,647 --> 00:14:08,813
The Root agent reads for an hour.

218
00:14:08,813 --> 00:14:15,506
Then, tired of standing, he does what nobody in the Leaf has ever done to a filing box. He sits on it.

219
00:14:15,724 --> 00:14:17,958
[CLONE] Boss. A man is using me as a stool.

220
00:14:18,082 --> 00:14:23,746
Boxes make no noise. This one remembers his hands, his boots and every page he opened.

221
00:14:23,746 --> 00:14:27,896
When he leaves, the clone pops. The only witness was furniture.

222
00:14:28,147 --> 00:14:31,692
Morning. The Hokage's office. Danzo doesn't knock.

223
00:14:31,692 --> 00:14:37,081
The Third doesn't look up from his pipe. Naruto, filing in the corner, does.

224
00:14:37,296 --> 00:14:42,690
[DANZO] Hiruzen. The Uzumaki boy should be trained properly. Root has the facilities.

225
00:14:42,808 --> 00:14:45,387
[HIRUZEN] No. Absolutely not.

226
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:50,499
[DANZO] You've given the Nine-Tails a library card. A child with that much access is a risk.

227
00:14:50,656 --> 00:14:53,400
[HIRUZEN] He has a staff form, actually.

228
00:14:53,526 --> 00:14:57,950
[DANZO] A form is paper. I'll requisition him through the council. Today.

229
00:14:58,064 --> 00:15:01,836
[HIRUZEN] Section three of the staff regulations.

230
00:15:01,836 --> 00:15:10,153
[HIRUZEN] Office staff answer to the Hokage and no one else. Not the council. Not Root. Not you.

231
00:15:10,265 --> 00:15:13,544
[NARUTO] I signed it twice by accident! Does that make it twice as binding?

232
00:15:13,672 --> 00:15:15,251
[HIRUZEN] I believe it does.

233
00:15:15,410 --> 00:15:18,449
[NARUTO] Also, one of your guys sat on a filing box last night.

234
00:15:18,449 --> 00:15:20,194
[NARUTO] It was me. I'd like an apology.

235
00:15:20,342 --> 00:15:21,756
[DANZO] I don't know what you mean.

236
00:15:21,892 --> 00:15:26,416
[NARUTO] Plain mask. Boots like a wet sandwich. Sat on me for an hour.

237
00:15:26,555 --> 00:15:28,484
[DANZO] He's a boy, Hiruzen.

238
00:15:28,636 --> 00:15:30,050
[HIRUZEN] He's my clerk.

239
00:15:30,195 --> 00:15:34,737
Danzo has a hundred ways around a rule. He has none around a form.

240
00:15:34,737 --> 00:15:43,959
Weeks ago, the Third Hokage filed the one document in Konoha that Root can't requisition. The old man didn't punish him. He hired him.

241
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:47,384
[HIRUZEN] He'll try again, Naruto.

242
00:15:47,514 --> 00:15:49,993
[NARUTO] I know. He'll have to fill out a form.

243
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:52,629
[HIRUZEN] I'm very proud of that form.

244
00:15:52,787 --> 00:15:56,673
Danzo leaves without raising his voice. He doesn't look angry.

245
00:15:56,673 --> 00:16:00,246
He looks like a man who has simply moved the appointment.

246
00:16:02,881 --> 00:16:08,246
The Third Hokage has an idea. Keep Team Seven busy and inside the village.

247
00:16:08,246 --> 00:16:14,480
So he hands them D-ranks. Weeding. Painting. Babysitting. And the occasional lost cat.

248
00:16:14,694 --> 00:16:21,446
Naruto sends two hundred clones. By noon, twelve missions are done. By three, twenty-nine.

249
00:16:21,446 --> 00:16:26,623
Every garden in Konoha has been weeded by someone with the same face.

250
00:16:26,867 --> 00:16:31,339
He hasn't gotten one ounce stronger. He has simply brought more of himself.

251
00:16:31,339 --> 00:16:36,706
Years from now he'll run the whole Hokage's office this way. Today it's the mission board.

252
00:16:36,928 --> 00:16:40,075
Eleven of the forty missions are the same cat.

253
00:16:40,075 --> 00:16:47,327
Tora, the Daimyo's wife's cat, escapes every week, and every week a team loses an afternoon and some skin.

254
00:16:47,551 --> 00:16:49,785
[CLONE] Boss, found the cat. Again.

255
00:16:49,915 --> 00:16:51,854
[NARUTO] Again? What number is this?

256
00:16:51,997 --> 00:16:54,556
[CLONE] Eleven. We know his hiding places better than he does.

257
00:16:54,671 --> 00:16:57,369
By the eleventh capture, the cat has given up.

258
00:16:57,369 --> 00:17:03,350
The Daimyo's wife squeezes it until its eyes go dead, and for once the whole room agrees with the cat.

259
00:17:03,596 --> 00:17:09,020
[IRUKA] Weeding, done. Painting, done. Grocery run for the Akimichi clan, done.

260
00:17:09,143 --> 00:17:11,862
[CLONE] That one was hard. They noticed we ate the potato chips.

261
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:18,019
[KAKASHI] Naruto. I notice the missions are finished before I find out what they are.

262
00:17:18,142 --> 00:17:19,691
[NARUTO] Efficiency, sensei!

263
00:17:19,819 --> 00:17:23,743
[KAKASHI] I've read four chapters. Don't stop on my account.

264
00:17:23,903 --> 00:17:28,387
[IRUKA] Team Seven. Forty D-ranks. In one day. That's the entire board.

265
00:17:28,515 --> 00:17:29,634
[SAKURA] I can't feel my arms.

266
00:17:29,772 --> 00:17:31,501
[SASUKE] Tch. Is that all there is?

267
00:17:31,658 --> 00:17:35,042
[KAKASHI] I'm up to chapter nine. Excellent day.

268
00:17:35,152 --> 00:17:38,641
[IRUKA] There are no more D-ranks. I'm out. I looked under the desk.

269
00:17:38,797 --> 00:17:44,716
[HIRUZEN] Then I suppose it's time for something harder. A C-rank. An escort.

270
00:17:44,865 --> 00:17:46,169
[NARUTO] Who's the client, old man?

271
00:17:46,308 --> 00:17:52,692
[HIRUZEN] A bridge builder from the Land of Waves. He's paying the going rate for a C-rank.

272
00:17:52,805 --> 00:17:53,564
[SASUKE] Finally.

273
00:17:53,706 --> 00:17:59,828
That night in the archive, Naruto reads the part of the bingo book nobody reads. The appendix.

274
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:05,820
The Hidden Mist's procedure for hunting their own missing ninja. It's written like a recipe.

275
00:18:06,029 --> 00:18:10,042
[CLONE] Step one, find the missing-nin. Step two, finish the missing-nin.

276
00:18:10,042 --> 00:18:12,758
[CLONE] Step three, destroy the body where it falls.

277
00:18:12,688 --> 00:18:17,507
[CLONE] There's a diagram. A body, a flame, and an arrow that says, here.

278
00:18:17,663 --> 00:18:18,697
[NARUTO] Why where it falls?

279
00:18:18,837 --> 00:18:21,776
[CLONE] Secrets. A hunter never carries the body home.

280
00:18:21,776 --> 00:18:24,331
[CLONE] It says so four times. Underlined twice.

281
00:18:24,261 --> 00:18:26,735
[CLONE] And somebody wrote in the margin, I mean it.

282
00:18:26,884 --> 00:18:31,523
[NARUTO] So they burn it right there. Nobody drags a body forty miles. I respect that.

283
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:37,260
It's the most boring paragraph in the book. Naruto folds the corner of the page anyway.

284
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:40,554
Boring paragraphs are where the useful things hide.

285
00:18:40,784 --> 00:18:43,536
The next morning, at the village gate.

286
00:18:43,536 --> 00:18:51,503
Team Seven, one jonin, and a bridge builder from the Land of Waves, with a hat, a bottle and a very calm face.

287
00:18:51,744 --> 00:18:54,055
[TAZUNA] I'm just a simple bridge builder.

288
00:18:54,055 --> 00:18:58,258
[TAZUNA] Nothing exciting is going to happen on this trip. I promise.

289
00:18:58,390 --> 00:19:01,074
[SAKURA] That's what a C-rank is, right? Nothing exciting?

290
00:19:01,205 --> 00:19:05,914
[KAKASHI] Stay close. It's an escort. Nothing dangerous. Probably.

291
00:19:06,032 --> 00:19:14,304
They walk out under the gate. For the first hour Naruto is quiet, which worries Kakashi more than any noise could.

292
00:19:14,304 --> 00:19:19,456
Behind them, a hundred clones hold the archive. Ahead, a long dry road.

293
00:19:19,695 --> 00:19:22,934
Dust. Cracked mud. Not a cloud since last week.

294
00:19:22,934 --> 00:19:28,999
And in the middle of the road, sitting there as if somebody left it behind, is a puddle.

295
00:19:29,247 --> 00:19:32,151
[NARUTO] Sensei. It hasn't rained in a week.

